<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pangeran Antasari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1809–1862</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pangeran Antasari was a prince of the Banjar Sultanate in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a> who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banjarmasin-war">Banjarmasin War</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> rule from 1859. His followers proclaimed him their leader with a religious title in 1862, but he died of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smallpox">smallpox</a> later that year; his descendants continued the resistance until 1905. He was declared a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-hero-of-indonesia">National Hero of Indonesia</a> in 1968.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pangeran-antasari.jpg" alt="Pangeran Antasari" width="320" height="412" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pangeran_Antasari_Museum_Lambung_Mangkurat.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
